{"name":"Caster Sugar","hex":"#ffffe8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"caster sugar","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Granulated sugar that has been sifted to have a finer crystal size, so that it can be shaken out of the holes of a caster."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/caster_sugar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sucrose","blocks":[{"text":"Sucrose is a disaccharide, a sugar composed of glucose and fructose subunits. It is produced naturally in plants and is the main constituent of white sugar. It has the molecular formula C12H22O11."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Saccharose2.svg/330px-Saccharose2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sucrose","wikidata":"Q4027534"},{"title":"Caster","blocks":[{"text":"A caster is an undriven wheel that is designed to be attached to the bottom of a larger object to enable that object to be moved."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Swivel_caster.jpg/330px-Swivel_caster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caster","wikidata":"Q1534874"},{"title":"Sugar","blocks":[{"text":"Sugar is a class of sweet-tasting, soluble carbohydrates, many of which are used in food. Simple sugars, also called monosaccharides, include glucose, fructose and galactose. Compound sugars, also called disaccharides or double sugars, are molecules made of two bonded monosaccharides; common examples are sucrose, lactose and maltose. White sugar is almost pure sucrose. During digestion, compound sugars are hydrolysed into simple sugars."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Sucre_blanc_cassonade_complet_rapadura.jpg/330px-Sucre_blanc_cassonade_complet_rapadura.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S